One important evaluator detail: leaderboard timing regenerates data and weights for each timed repeat. That means cached transposed/packed weights often miss, so the current code pays weight conversion inside the timed call. I’m measuring cache-miss costs now and will prefer kernels that consume the original FP32 weights directly where that wins.
