This profiling run is on a correctness-only fallback case, but it isolates the split output pattern using the same hidden size and output dimension. If the final cuBLAS projection is materially faster, I’ll port that split into the FP16 benchmark path.
codex
There is already an unused Triton kernel that fuses input layernorm with the five projections. It trades less memory traffic for more registers and less parallelism, so I’m benchmarking it by shape before deciding whether to route any benchmark cases through it.
