A lower-risk numerical approximation is to evaluate the gate sigmoid from FP16-rounded logits instead of full FP32 logits. The gates are already stored as FP16 afterward, and current max errors have margin, so I’m testing whether that trims projection/gate time without breaking the `2e-2` tolerance.
