codex
Native LayerNorm is much slower. I’m adding a Triton single-load LayerNorm variant instead: it keeps one full channel row tile in registers, computes mean/variance, and stores FP16. That can reduce input reads versus the current two-pass row kernel for `dim=128/384`.
apply patch
